<title>SOUTH AFRICA: CRICKET-CLOSE OF PLAY SCORES/RESULTS IN SUPERSPORT SERIES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-CLOSE OF PLAY SCORES/RESULTS IN SUPERSPORT SERIES.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results and close of play</p>
<p>scores on the third day of the Supersport series cricket matches</p>
<p>on Sunday.</p>
<p>In Bloemfontein: Free State 251 and 246 (Deon Jordaan 66,</p>
<p>Kosie Venter 57). Transvaal 197 and 108 (Nico Pretorius 4-26).</p>
<p>Free State won by 192 runs.</p>
<p>In Kimberley: Griqualand West 298 and 167 (Brett Schultz</p>
<p>5-49). Western Province 470-5 declared (John Commins 200 not</p>
<p>out, Desmond Haynes 91). Western Province won by an innings and</p>
<p>five runs.</p>
<p>In East London: Border 331 and 201-4 (Mark Boucher 68 not</p>
<p>out, Brad White 54). Boland 277 (Wayne Truter 95, Andrew Wylie</p>
<p>74).</p>
<p>In Port Elizabeth: Eastern Province 265 and 118 (Pat Symcox</p>
<p>4-26). Natal 429 (Errol Stewart 138, Jonty Rhodes 108). Natal</p>
<p>won by an innings and 46 runs.</p>
</text>
